---
interface Props { kind: 'physical' | 'failover' | 'placement' | 'commit' }
const { kind } = Astro.props;
---
{kind === 'physical' && <figure class="pg-scale-plate">
 <div class="flow"><div class="machine"><h3>Primary A</h3><div class="stage">Backend commits<br/><strong>price 25</strong></div><span class="arrow">↓ WAL records</span><div class="stage">WAL sender<br/><small>reads the log stream</small></div></div><div class="pg-scale-transfer">WAL stream <span>→</span></div><div class="machine"><h3>Standby B</h3><div class="stage">WAL receiver<br/><strong>flush covers marker M</strong></div><span class="arrow">↓ replay paused here</span><div class="stage old">Startup process / replay<br/><strong>has not reached M</strong></div><span class="arrow">↓ new read</span><div class="result">price <strong>20</strong></div></div></div>
 <figcaption>The receiver can continue while replay is paused. The standby has the log needed for price 25, but its current queryable state still has price 20. M is a position captured after the primary commit.</figcaption>
</figure>}
{kind === 'failover' && <figure class="pg-scale-plate">
 <div class="origin">Shared history: <strong>price 27</strong></div><div class="fork"><div class="branch abandoned"><span class="arrow">↙ old timeline</span><h3>A accepts price 35</h3><p>B was stopped and never received it.</p><div class="stage">A is stopped before promotion</div><span class="arrow">↓ rewind discards divergence</span><div class="result">A rejoins with <strong>27</strong></div></div><div class="branch"><span class="arrow">↘ new timeline</span><h3>B is promoted with 27</h3><p>Surviving history becomes authoritative.</p><div class="stage">New write: price <strong>30</strong></div><span class="arrow">↓ streams to rejoined A</span><div class="result">Both now read <strong>30</strong></div></div></div>
 <figcaption>Observed in two isolated PostgreSQL 18 servers. Rewind follows B’s history; it does not preserve A’s unreplicated price 35. Stopping A supplies fencing in this controlled experiment.</figcaption>
</figure>}
{kind === 'placement' && <figure class="pg-scale-plate">
 <div class="origin">Query: <code>tenant_id = 7</code><br/><small>Hash tenant → shard range → worker placement</small></div><div class="route">↙ route this request <span>other tenant work ↘</span></div><div class="workers"><div class="machine"><h3>Worker A · tenant 7</h3><div class="record teal">customers shard<br/><strong>(7, 1) Ada</strong></div><div class="join">↑ same (tenant, customer) ↓</div><div class="record teal">orders shard<br/><strong>(7, 101) customer 1 · 25</strong></div><div class="result">Local join → Ada, 25</div></div><div class="machine"><h3>Worker B · tenant 8</h3><div class="record amber">customers shard<br/><strong>(8, 1) Bo</strong></div><div class="join">↑ same (tenant, customer) ↓</div><div class="record amber">orders shard<br/><strong>(8, 102) customer 1 · 40</strong></div><div class="result">Not contacted for tenant 7</div></div></div>
 <figcaption>Schematic Citus placement, not measured shard IDs. Matching distribution ranges keep each tenant’s two table fragments together. Real shards commonly contain several tenants; co-location does not require a shard per tenant.</figcaption>
</figure>}
{kind === 'commit' && <figure class="pg-scale-plate">
 <p class="plate-title">One transaction adds a row on each worker</p><ol class="commit-stages"><li><span class="number">1</span><div><strong>Prepare both workers</strong><div class="pair"><span>A: row prepared, invisible</span><span>B: row prepared, invisible</span></div></div></li><li><span class="number">2</span><div><strong>Record the commit decision</strong><p>The coordinator durably chooses commit.</p></div></li><li><span class="number">3</span><div><strong>Deliver that decision</strong><div class="pair"><span>A: committed, visible</span><span class="old">B: still prepared</span></div><p>A query taking snapshots now can see only A’s new row.</p></div></li><li><span class="number">4</span><div><strong>Finish every participant</strong><div class="pair"><span>A: committed, visible</span><span>B: committed, visible</span></div></div></li></ol>
 <figcaption>A possible two-phase commit schedule, not a timing measurement. Recovery can complete the durable decision after a failure. That atomic outcome does not make independently taken worker snapshots simultaneous.</figcaption>
</figure>}
<style>
 .pg-scale-plate{--pg-paper:#f7f3e9;--pg-ink:#3b3a35;--pg-line:#9b978b;--pg-teal:#dceae4;--pg-amber:#eee2cb;background:var(--pg-paper);color:var(--pg-ink);border:1px solid var(--pg-line);padding:clamp(1rem,3vw,1.8rem);margin:2rem 0;font-family:var(--font-sans,system-ui,sans-serif);font-size:.94rem;line-height:1.5}
 @media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.pg-scale-plate{--pg-paper:#292b29;--pg-ink:#ebe7db;--pg-line:#77786d;--pg-teal:#29463e;--pg-amber:#4e4330}}
 .pg-scale-plate h3{font-size:1rem;margin:0 0 1rem;line-height:1.5;color:inherit}.pg-scale-plate p{font-size:inherit;line-height:1.5;margin:.5rem 0}.pg-scale-plate small{font-size:.85rem}.flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 6rem 1fr;align-items:start}.machine{border:1px solid var(--pg-line);padding:1rem;min-width:0}.stage,.record{border-block:1px solid var(--pg-line);padding:.65rem;background:var(--pg-teal)}.old,.amber{background:var(--pg-amber)}.arrow,.join{display:block;padding:.6rem 0;text-align:center;font-size:.86rem}.pg-scale-transfer{text-align:center;padding-top:5rem;font-size:.8rem}.pg-scale-transfer span{display:block;font-size:2rem}.result{padding:.65rem 0 0;border-bottom:2px solid var(--pg-line)}.origin{text-align:center;border-bottom:1px solid var(--pg-line);padding:0 0 1rem}.fork,.workers{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem}.branch{border-left:2px solid var(--pg-line);padding:0 1rem}.abandoned{border-left-style:dashed}.route{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:.83rem;padding:.7rem 0}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.6rem;margin-top:.5rem}.pair span{padding:.7rem;border:1px solid var(--pg-line)}.commit-stages{list-style:none;padding:0!important;display:grid;gap:1rem;margin:1rem 0}.commit-stages li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.6rem 1fr;gap:.7rem;margin:0!important}.number{border-top:1px solid var(--pg-line);font-family:monospace}.plate-title{font-weight:600}.pg-scale-plate figcaption{font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.6;margin:1.2rem 0 0;color:inherit}
 @media(max-width:600px){.flow,.fork,.workers{grid-template-columns:1fr}.pg-scale-transfer{padding:.5rem;display:flex;gap:.7rem;justify-content:center;align-items:center}.pg-scale-transfer span{transform:rotate(90deg);font-size:1.5rem}.route span{display:none}.pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}.machine{padding:.8rem}.branch{padding:.6rem 0 .6rem .8rem}}
</style>
